\section{Results}

\subsection{High-detail input enables source-specific tag retrieval}

At a 512-token cap, Qwen strict value-tag F1 is @@E2_LOW@@ at 768 and
@@E2_HIGH@@ at 3072, a difference of @@E2@@ (@@E2_CI@@). The 768 condition
reaches the cap on @@E2_LOW_CAP@@ of records, yet raising its cap from 192 to
512 does not recover exact value answers. The Set B high-minus-low effect is
@@E2_192@@ (@@E2_192_CI@@) at the original 192-token cap and @@E2@@
(@@E2_CI@@) at 512. The pre-specified seed-29 and seed-31 source partitions
retain effects of @@E6_29@@ (@@E6_29_CI@@) and @@E6_31@@ (@@E6_31_CI@@),
respectively (Figure~\ref{fig:robustness}). All four contrasts are positive;
the source partitions remain descriptive sensitivity analyses rather than
independent replications.

\begin{figure}[H]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{figure_2_tag_reading_robustness_v5.pdf}
\caption{Tag-reading robustness. Panel A shows the high-detail and
counterfactual-image effects. Panel B retains both output caps and both
pre-specified source partitions. Intervals use 10,000 source-cluster bootstrap
replicates.}
\label{fig:robustness}
\end{figure}

\subsection{Correct and counterfactual images establish visual grounding}

At the 3072-side, 192-token operating point, correct-image precision, recall,
F1, and exact-set accuracy are @@QWEN_P@@, @@QWEN_R@@, @@QWEN_F1@@, and
@@QWEN_EXACT@@. The same questions yield F1 @@SHUFFLED_F1@@ with a
source-shuffled image and @@TEXT_F1@@ without an image. Correct minus shuffled
is @@E3@@ (@@E3_CI@@), and correct minus no image is @@E8@@ (@@E8_CI@@).
Thus, the large tag signal follows the requested drawing rather than merely
the prompt or the presence of arbitrary P\&ID pixels.

Figure~\ref{fig:evidence-ladder} makes the comparison inspectable. Under the
frozen minimum-hash rule, only the correctly paired 3072 input returns the
complete reference set; the lower-detail, source-shuffled, and no-image
conditions produce zero tag F1. The selection rule is deterministic, and the
complete drawing is shown because public records provide no tag coordinates.

