PaddleOCR attains higher precision than Qwen, while Qwen recovers a different
fraction of the reference tags. Their set union raises recall to @@UNION_R@@
and F1 to @@UNION_F1@@; its F1 increment over Qwen is @@UNION_QWEN_DIFF@@
(@@UNION_QWEN_DIFF_CI@@). The union-minus-OCR difference is
@@UNION_OCR_DIFF@@ (@@UNION_OCR_DIFF_CI@@), whose interval crosses zero. Set
intersection reaches precision @@INTERSECTION_P@@, providing a high-confidence
shortlist at lower recall. The OCR-first fallback reaches F1
@@OCR_FALLBACK_F1@@ and exact-set accuracy @@OCR_FALLBACK_EXACT@@. These
truth-free rules define useful retrieval modes rather than a learned ensemble.
Because the rule family was analysed after the component results, the fusion
comparison remains descriptive.

